## Summary of the Frozen ISA

- 32-bit load–store machine, byte-addressed, little-endian, fixed 32-bit instructions in RV32I-derived formats.
- 16 general-purpose registers (x0–x15), so register fields are 4 bits wide. x0 (`lefela`) is hard-wired to zero; x2 is the stack pointer (`mokgethi`).
- Sesotho assembly mnemonics, for example `eketsa` (add), `eketsa-haufi` (addi), `fokotsa` (sub), `kenya` (lw), `boloka` (sw) and `hlahloba` (beq).
- I-type immediates range from -2048 to 2047.
- Branches are resolved in the EX stage; a taken branch flushes two instructions (A6c).

